{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"normal","reason":"Routine command cleanup can select and kill unrelated processes owned by the same user based on their working directory and start time."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A transient cleanup failure during a gate timeout rerun aborts the run instead of retrying or recovering to another implementation round."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A background writer with a replaced environment can survive cleanup and continue modifying the worktree after the command reports success."}]}